---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/editorial-policy/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">Editorial Policy &amp; Source Standards</span>
      </nav>
      <article class="content-narrow prose">
        <div class="eyebrow">Otto by Tebra</div>
        <h1>Editorial Policy & Source Standards</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Practice guidance should make its sources and limits easy to find.
        </p>
        <h2>Use named, relevant sources.</h2>
        <p>
          Regulatory and billing statements link to government guidance or the
          documentation of the product being described. Worked examples are
          labeled hypothetical. We separate a calculator’s output from a market
          benchmark or prediction.
        </p>
        <h2>Show the author and review date.</h2>
        <p>
          Articles display an organizational byline, source-check date, and
          links to supporting material. A named reviewer is added only after
          that person has completed and approved the review. No expert review is
          claimed for the current drafts.
        </p>
        <h2>Keep product claims specific.</h2>
        <p>
          Product pages describe publicly documented workflows. Unverified
          pricing, security, or availability details stay explicit. We do not
          treat standalone tools as evidence of integrated EHR capabilities.
        </p>
        <h2>Check changes before publication.</h2>
        <p>
          Confirm product and competitor descriptions against current
          documentation. Review legal, coding, and financial guidance with the
          appropriate owner. Update both the visible page and its structured
          data when the underlying facts change.
        </p>
        <h2>Current collection status.</h2>
        <p>
          This is an internal review edition prepared October 16, 2026. The
          content was drafted with AI assistance using Mateo’s package and the
          linked sources. Final editorial approval, specialist review, and the
          author assignment are pending.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
